* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-closed-loop-lock (issue #37, Part of #16)
* PART B -- PROPOSAL closed-loop PLL transient.
* spec/porting-plan.md rows 7 (lock time), 10 (reference spur), 11 (power).
*
* ===========================================================================
* THIS DECK IS **NOT** THE COMMITTED DESIGN. READ THIS BEFORE QUOTING IT.
* ===========================================================================
* It differs from Part A (`tb_pll_closed.sp.tmpl`, the as-drawn loop) in
* exactly two deliberate, separately-motivated ways, and in nothing else:
*
*   1. LOOP FILTER RESIZED. `XR1`'s `rppd` length is @R1L@ instead of the
*      as-drawn 120u. At 2400u this is the `R1` x20 proposal that
*      ../../sg13cmos5l-loop-bandwidth-pm/corners/proposal.csv identified as
*      the widest-margin filter/trim pair (PM 58.6-61.8 deg at every PVT
*      bundle). It is still the real `rppd` compact model -- the resistor is
*      lengthened, not replaced by an ideal element.
*
*   2. BEHAVIOURAL DIVIDER. The feedback divider is an XSPICE `d_dff` toggle
*      chain (divide-by-64), NOT the committed `divider_chain` block. This
*      is forced, not chosen: Part A measures that the as-drawn
*      `divider_chain` does not divide at all, and
*      ../records/RECORD-001 localises that to `dff_tg_hv`'s hold path. A
*      loop built on a divider that does not divide cannot produce a lock
*      time, so this deck substitutes an ideal divider of the SAME ratio the
*      as-drawn chain has with P5..P0 = 000000 (N = 2^6 = 64) in order to
*      answer the separate question "do the loop dynamics work once the
*      divider does". The substitution is labelled here and in the record,
*      and every number this deck produces is reported as a PROPOSAL number.
*
* Everything else -- `pfd`, `cp`, `vco`, `lock_detector`, the per-domain
* supplies, the testbench-local cascode bias replica, the lumped-MOM-cap
* host constraint, and the testbench-local integration wiring -- is
* IDENTICAL to Part A. See `tb_pll_closed.sp.tmpl`'s header for all of it;
* it is not repeated here.
*
* `../testbench/run.sh` substitutes @CORNER_MOS@, @CORNER_RES@, @TEMP@,
* @VDD@, @TREF@/@TREFH@, @IREF@, @B0V@/@B1V@, @VC0@, @R1L@, @TSTOP@,
* @TPRINT@, @TMAX@ and @TAVG0@ per ../corners/matrix.md.

.lib $PDK_ROOT/$PDK/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.lib $PDK_ROOT/$PDK/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib @CORNER_RES@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@
.global sub!

.include pll_blocks_prop.spice

Vsub sub! 0 dc 0

* --- per-domain supplies (row 11: one deck, one operating point) ---
Vdd_pfd vdd_pfd 0 dc @VDD@
Vdd_cp  vdd_cp  0 dc @VDD@
Vdd_vco vdd_vco 0 dc @VDD@
Vdd_ld  vdd_ld  0 dc @VDD@
Vddrep  vddrep  0 dc @VDD@

Vref ref 0 pulse(0 @VDD@ 0 100p 100p @TREFH@ @TREF@)
Vb0 b0 0 dc @B0V@
Vb1 b1 0 dc @B1V@

* --- testbench-local cascode mirror reference for the charge pump ---
XMREFP1 nrp1 nbp  vddrep vddrep sg13_hv_pmos w=24u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMREFP2 nbp  nbp  nrp1   vddrep sg13_hv_pmos w=24u l=1u ng=1 m=1
Irefp nbp 0 dc @IREF@
XMREFN1 nrn1 nbn  0 0 sg13_hv_nmos w=8u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMREFN2 nbn  nbn  nrn1 0 sg13_hv_nmos w=8u l=1u ng=1 m=1
Irefn 0 nbn dc @IREF@

* --- real blocks ---
XPFD ref fb up dn vdd_pfd 0 pfd
XCP up dn nbp nbp nbn nbn vctrl vdd_cp 0 cp
XLF vctrl 0 loop_filter
XVCO vctrl b0 b1 clk vdd_vco 0 vco
XLD up dn lock vdd_ld 0 lock_detector

* --- BEHAVIOURAL divide-by-64 (see header item 2) ---
.model dffb d_dff(clk_delay=20p set_delay=20p reset_delay=20p ic=0
+ rise_delay=20p fall_delay=20p)
.model adcb adc_bridge(in_low=1.40 in_high=1.90)
.model dacb dac_bridge(out_low=0 out_high=@VDD@ out_undef=1.65
+ t_rise=80p t_fall=80p)
Aad [clk] [dclk] adcb
Ab1 q1b dclk NULL NULL q1 q1b dffb
Ab2 q2b q1   NULL NULL q2 q2b dffb
Ab3 q3b q2   NULL NULL q3 q3b dffb
Ab4 q4b q3   NULL NULL q4 q4b dffb
Ab5 q5b q4   NULL NULL q5 q5b dffb
Ab6 q6b q5   NULL NULL q6 q6b dffb
Ada [q6] [fb] dacb

.ic v(vctrl)=@VC0@
.ic v(xvco.ring1)=0.5

.tran @TPRINT@ @TSTOP@ 0 @TMAX@

.control
run
meas tran i_pfd avg i(Vdd_pfd) from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran i_cp  avg i(Vdd_cp)  from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran i_vco avg i(Vdd_vco) from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran i_ld  avg i(Vdd_ld)  from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran vc_avg avg v(vctrl) from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran vc_max max v(vctrl) from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran vc_min min v(vctrl) from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
print i_pfd i_cp i_vco i_ld vc_avg vc_max vc_min
linearize v(ref) v(fb) v(vctrl) v(clk) v(lock)
wrdata wave.dat v(ref) v(fb) v(vctrl) v(clk) v(lock)
.endc
.end
